WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.249 --> 00:00:04.950
Let's go right to the phones at 6 1 7 8 3
0 0.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.880
Forty seven fifty.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.130
We are going to start today with our caller
from the for a zero area code.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.460
Who's calling today from 4 8 0.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.340
Hi, David, is this me?

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.340
Yes, it is.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.340
What's your name?

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.410
Hi, my name is Joseph.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.210
Hey, Joe, what's up?

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.720
Hey, so I've been a big fan.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:31.090
I first heard about you on Joe Rogan and just
had a quick question.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:36.950
So there doesn't appear to be any official
or constitutional mandate that the incumbent

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:43.350
president is required to hold a debate with
the opposing party's nominee.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.350
Right.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:49.800
Trump seems to gravitate toward controversy
and undermining our institutions.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.289
And we're seeing in real time how he's trying
to propagate conspiracy theories about the

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.380
Obama Obama-Biden administration.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.380
Yep.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.920
How likely is it that as a strategy to undercut
Biden, Trump forgoes debating Biden altogether?

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.960
Listen, he's hinted at he can do as many debates
as he wants or none at all.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.590
And it shouldn't be up to the Commission on
Presidential Debates to decide that that's

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.439
sort of been his thing like that.

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:21.630
He says he and the opponent, whoever at the
time we didn't know who it was going to be,

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.270
should just be able to sort it out and do
whatever they want, but that the Commission

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.909
on Presidential Debates shouldn't get to intervene.

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:32.090
I think there's only about a 15 percent chance
that this is just me pulling a number that

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.329
Trump just refuses to debate altogether.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:42.390
I don't see it as particularly likely, especially
because I think Trump sees himself as winning

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.049
the debates for sure.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:48.420
And so I have a hard time imagining he'll
really go through with this, not doing the

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.420
debates.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:55.600
But it's not completely outside the realm
of possibility.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.600
OK.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.960
If you don't mind and I just want to maybe
another question.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:05.760
Do you think that with the lack of the campaign
rallies because of the pandemic right now,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.800
that it's going to hurt Joe's chances of winning
over voters?

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.800
Not on balance.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.580
I mean, listen, the polls only give us a snapshot
of what's going on right now.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.230
Trump's been failing on Corona virus and Biden's
just been doing interviews from his house.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.360
And Biden right now is doing fine in the polls.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:33.860
I think that the risk to Joe Biden is if Trump
starts doing rallies again, particularly in

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:39.730
battleground states and Joe Biden, because
the public health officials say that this

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.080
is probably not a good idea.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.370
Joe Biden abides by it.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.819
That's where you could see it start to hurt
Joe Biden.

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:47.420
But right now, I don't think it's hurt him.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.550
And I don't think we can really find data
that suggests that it has.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.280
You so much.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.360
All right, appreciate the call.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:55.700
Thank you.

